Description: CVE-2026-56154 - mod_rewrite: copy lookahead vary_this value
 When evaluating %{LA-U:...} and %{LA-F:...} lookahead variables, mod_rewrite
 runs the lookup against a sub-request and then destroys it. ctx->vary_this
 may point to memory allocated from the sub-request pool, which is freed by
 ap_destroy_sub_req(), leaving a dangling pointer (use after free). Duplicate
 the value into the main request pool before the sub-request is destroyed.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/apache/httpd/commit/6e4d1e614597109909dda495d235b6a1331d7beb
